4. Sync and Cache DesignFirst Sync: Initiated upon explicit user consent. Downloads full baseline JSON payloads from MSRC, CISA KEV, NVD (paginated within 120-day windows), and Winbindex snapshot.Incremental Sync: Utilizes stored retrieval timestamps and lastModStartDate parameters to fetch only delta updates.Offline Behaviour: The tool operates 100% offline using local SQLite / LMDB caches after the first sync. Network calls are bypassed entirely unless a manual refresh is requested.Staleness Display: The UI displays a clear freshness indicator: Cache Status: Synchronized [Date] (X days old). If cache age exceeds 30 days, a non-blocking warning banner suggests an optional sync.Cache Size Caps: Local cache storage is hard-capped at 5 GB. LRU (Least Recently Used) eviction applies to binary symbol caches, while core KB/CVE catalog records are permanently retained unless manually purged.Integrity Hashes: Every cached file and JSON payload is verified against a computed SHA-256 integrity hash upon read.5. Join AlgorithmThe correlator joins data across heterogeneous sources using the following deterministic sequence:Input Selection: User selects target KB (e.g., KB5126836).MSRC Resolution: Query local cache for KbRecord. Extract list of associated cveId values. If missing from cache and user consent is granted, query MSRC API.Vulnerability Enrichment: For each cveId, query local CveRecord store for CVSS, CWE, and CISA KEV status (kevListed).Binary Pairing: Query Winbindex local index for BuildRecord entries matching the KB ID. Group binaries into older version (pre-KB) and newer version (post-KB) pairs based on windowsVersion and timestamp.Failure Mode Handling & UI Representation:Superseded KB: If KB is superseded, UI displays: Notice: This KB has been superseded by [Newer KB]. Results reflect historical baseline.Multiple Products: If a CVE maps to multiple products, UI groups findings by product CPE tree to prevent false attribution.Missing Fixed Build: If binary data is absent, UI displays: UNVERIFIED_BUILD: Binary change data not indexed for this update. CVE fixed via configuration or servicing stack. (Never represented as negative or safe).Policy-Only Fix: If no binary changed, UI displays: POLICY_ONLY: Security update enforces policy/registry change without PE binary modification.6. Error Handling TableConditionUser-Visible MessageRetry PolicyNetwork TimeoutConnection timed out reaching [Source]. Operating in offline mode using cached data.Exponential backoff (3 attempts, max 30s delay)HTTP 429 Rate LimitedRate limit exceeded by [Source]. Pausing sync operations automatically.Wait 30 seconds, single retry, then prompt userInvalid JSON SchemaReceived malformed data payload from [Source]. Response discarded for security.No retry; log parse exception internallyTLS / Certificate ErrorSecure connection failed due to certificate validation failure. Request aborted.No retry; abort operationCache Integrity FailureLocal cache corruption detected for record [ID]. Rebuilding index segment.Single local cache rebuild from backup store7. SecurityUntrusted Input Rules: All external JSON and binary feeds are treated as untrusted. No remote code execution, dynamic script evaluation, or arbitrary deserialization is permitted.Size & Time Caps: HTTP response bodies are strictly capped at 50 MB per request. Stream parsing (e.g., ijson) is used for large JSON catalogs. Connection and read timeouts are hard-capped at 15 seconds.Strict JSON: Parsers operate in strict RFC 8259 mode with duplicate key rejection and comment stripping disabled.Redirects & TLS: HTTP redirects (3xx) are limited to a maximum of 3 hops. TLS 1.3 is enforced as default, with TLS 1.2 as minimum allowable; certificate pinning or strict system trust store validation is mandatory.No Execution: Downloaded PE binaries (.exe, .dll, .sys) and PDBs are strictly stored as raw byte arrays or analyzed statically via read-only parsers. They are never executed, loaded, or spawned.8. Test PlanFixtures Needed:Mock MSRC CVRF JSON responses with edge-case CVE mappings and superseded KBs.Truncated and malformed JSON payloads to test parser resilience.Mock Winbindex records with missing build timestamps and overlapping file hashes.Adversarial Inputs:Oversized JSON payloads (>50 MB) to verify size-cap rejection.Deeply nested JSON structures to prevent stack-overflow vulnerabilities.Malformed CVE strings and SQL injection strings injected into query parameters.Property Tests:Invariant: For any successfully ingested KbRecord, all associated cveId strings must resolve to a valid CveRecord or an explicit unresolved state.Invariant: Cache read after write must preserve SHA-256 integrity hashes across all record types.9. Open Decisions for the Product OwnerDecision: Should CISA KEV synchronization occur automatically in the background on startup when online?Recommendation: No. Background network activity violates the core offline-first and explicit-consent architecture. Sync must remain strictly manual or user-triggered.Decision: Should the local cache support AES-256 encryption at rest?Recommendation: Yes. Encrypting the local LMDB/SQLite cache protects intelligence data and parsed vulnerability metadata against local forensic inspection on analyst workstations.Decision: How should the tool handle conflicting CVSS scores between MSRC and NVD?Recommendation: Display both with attribution. Show MSRC's vendor assessment alongside NVD's scoring to provide complete context to the security analyst.10. SourcesMicrosoft Security Response Center API Documentation ([https://api.msrc.microsoft.com](https://api.msrc.microsoft.com))CISA Known Exploited Vulnerabilities Catalog ([https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog](https://www.cisa.gov/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog))NIST National Vulnerability Database API 2.0 ([https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/vulnerabilities](https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/vulnerabilities))Winbindex GitHub Repository ([https://github.com/m417z/winbindex](https://github.com/m417z/winbindex))Microsoft Symbol Server Documentation ([https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols](https://msdl.microsoft.com/download/symbols))Unverified Items ListMSRC API Exact Rate Limit Thresholds: Exact numerical rate limit ceilings for unauthenticated vs authenticated callers on api.msrc.microsoft.com are dynamically governed by Azure API Management and were not explicitly published in static documentation.Microsoft Update Catalog Proprietary Backend Endpoints: Direct SOAP/WSDL backend endpoint specifications for programmatic search against the Microsoft Update Catalog (as no public machine-readable REST API exists for it).
